---
// Lifts Starlight's content width on the page that includes it, so the page takes the room between its sidebars
// (the user, 2026-11-22): a kind's list, for more columns, and an entity page, for its wide tables (a stage's enemies).
// Starlight widens the "On this page" column to centre a page of its content width; here that column keeps the left
// sidebar's width and the content takes the rest. `--sl-content-width` itself stays, since the header centres the
// search over it, which would move between pages. Starlight's rules are in a cascade layer, so these win.
---

<style is:global>
	.sl-container {
		max-width: none;
	}
	@media (min-width: 72rem) {
		.right-sidebar-container {
			width: var(--sl-sidebar-width);
		}
		:root[data-has-sidebar][data-has-toc] .main-pane {
			width: calc(100% - var(--sl-sidebar-width));
		}
	}
</style>
